We went in with that fully formed pitch sheet.
我们带着完全成型的提案大纲去的。

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:22.579
We had, we had each character, and you write up a little description of each character, maybe eight or ten episode ideas, just in the shape of how the storytelling work, when you pitch them sort of like 15 or 20 minutes of like through this pitch document, you're going to give them a flavor of what it will be.
我们有，我们有每个角色，你们会写下每个角色的简单描述，大概八到十个分集创意，只是关于叙事方式的构想，当你们向他们推销时，大概花15或20分钟通过这份提案文件，让他们感受到这部剧会是什么样。

00:07:22.579 --> 00:07:26.139
And by far the best response in the room was CBS.
而到目前为止，房间里反应最好的就是CBS。

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:34.699
These wonderful women of CBS who got the emotion and the heart behind you, 20 trillion, Julie Pernworth, Edie Mendoza, and they got what this was.
CBS这些出色的女士们，她们理解你们背后的情感和真心，两万亿，朱莉·佩恩沃思（Julie Pernworth）、埃迪·门多萨（Edie Mendoza），她们懂这是什么。

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:49.300
And they had just been in a meeting with their higher ups there where they all, the directive was we want a younger, basically we want it from, we want friends, which we did not want to a come and just give them a friend's clone, but it definitely helped us that CBS wanted a friend.
她们刚和那里的高层开完会，高层给出的指令是，我们想要一个更年轻的，基本上我们希望它像，我们想要一部《老友记》，我们绝对不想来这里只是给他们一部《老友记》的复制品，但CBS想要一部《老友记》确实对我们很有帮助。

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:53.060
It was, I believe it was like really, it was like hauntingly good timing.
那是，我相信这真的是，时机好得令人发指。

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.060
Like it was, it was like that morning, they had had a meeting.
就像是，就像那天早上，他们刚开过会。

